  "published": "2026-09-18T14:36:06.877Z",
  "releaseNotes": "* Client: replies split across TCP reads no longer corrupt the connection\n      * Client: fixed sporadic ConnectAsync timeout when the PLC answers very fast\n      * Client: unknown COTP parameters in the connection confirm are skipped (receive thread hung before)\n      * Client: ReadBlocksOfTypeAsync / ReadBlocksCountAsync returned one entry too few\n      * Client: fixed NullReferenceException on ack for alarm indication subscription\n      * Server: RequestItem.TransportSize is public, ToTag renders bit requests as bit tags (e.g. DB100.2,x3,1)\n      * Server: fixed dropped connections under load, \"Collection was modified\" on DisconnectAsync and Critical log on stop\n      * Server: no reconnect attempts to disconnected clients anymore, their connections are closed\n      * Server: always answers jobs (HardwareFault if the data provider fails)\n      * Server: unknown COTP parameters in the connection request are skipped\n      * see CHANGELOG.md for details",
